From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 09 Nov 2026 18:13:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: encrypt EAPOL renewal on native-WiFi vdevs

The encrypted EAPOL conversion is gated by Ethernet encapsulation offload.
QCN9274 HW1 firmware without that service therefore sends PTK renewal M1
as native-WiFi with no per-frame RAW cipher override. Initial association
works, but the encrypted renewal times out and disconnects the station.

Use the existing cipher-specific IV/ICV conversion and extension descriptor
for encrypted EAPOL even when the vdev uses native-WiFi encapsulation.
Preserve the normal native-WiFi data path and the unencrypted handshake.

On BE10000 ES with QCN9274 HW1, three successive 20-second PTK renewals
and a 70-second zero-loss ping pass. Disabling this change in the same
module reproduces the M1 timeout and disconnection.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/dp_tx.c
@@ -254,7 +254,9 @@
 	switch (ti.encap_type) {
 	case HAL_TCL_ENCAP_TYPE_NATIVE_WIFI:
 		is_null_frame = ieee80211_is_nullfunc(hdr->frame_control);
-		if (ahvif->vif->offload_flags & IEEE80211_OFFLOAD_ENCAP_ENABLED) {
+		if ((ahvif->vif->offload_flags & IEEE80211_OFFLOAD_ENCAP_ENABLED) ||
+		    (skb->protocol == cpu_to_be16(ETH_P_PAE) &&
+		     (skb_cb->flags & ATH12K_SKB_CIPHER_SET))) {
 			if ((skb->protocol == cpu_to_be16(ETH_P_PAE) &&
 			     !(skb_cb->flags & ATH12K_SKB_CIPHER_SET)) || is_null_frame)
 				is_diff_encap = true;
@@ -276,9 +278,9 @@
 						ath12k_dp_tx_get_encrypt_type(skb_cb->cipher);
 				}
 			}
-			/* Firmware expects msdu ext descriptor for nwifi/raw packets
-			 * received in ETH mode. Without this, observed tx fail for
-			 * Multicast packets in ETH mode.
+			/* Firmware needs an extension for the per-frame RAW cipher
+			 * override, including EAPOL renewal on native-WiFi vdevs.
+			 * ETH-mode native-WiFi frames also need the extension.
 			 */
 			msdu_ext_desc = true;
 		} else {
